ROMAN-0972 -- control variates on the gauntlet's SPA gate (sealed file: external_gauntlet.py).
Uses libs/validation/control_variates.py (#245); v3 imports it inside the try, so this applies safely
in either order (before #245 the stage records UNMEASURED).

What it does: re-runs Hansen's SPA on the same 1,000 stationary-bootstrap draws (seed 0) with
exact-expectation control variates (u_k, u_k^2 for the top 8 strategies; cross-fitted beta and
an out-of-fold use decision, so the estimate is exactly unbiased) and RECORDS it beside the raw
verdict. v2 (audit 2026-10-07): RECORD-ONLY. The controlled p never changes spa_ok, in either
direction; `would_change` marks where it disagrees, so no veto is added without a missed-growth
line. Any error in the control-variate path is recorded as UNMEASURED. The raw p_value is unchanged and is
asserted reproduced bit-for-bit before the controlled side is allowed to act. The stage gains a
"control_variate" record (absent for a single-strategy matrix, so that stage is byte-identical).

Measured effect on the sealed trap suite (run_sealed_suite_lockbox.py 0 1000, union ledger
234,977 trials, tree 2d61e69a19):
    unpatched  genuine 52/600, traps 0/1500
    patched    genuine 52/600, traps 0/1500, 0 of 2,100 verdicts differ (v1; v2 cannot differ)
Every one of the 33 docket matrices has raw SPA p <= 0.001 (32 at 0.000), so the controlled
estimate has nothing to resolve there: no fold measures a gain out of fold, p_controlled is
None and the raw number stands. The patch is inert on this suite and only acts on dockets whose SPA p sits near
0.05. Tests run with the patch loaded: tests/research/test_adversary.py,
desks/mt5/tests/test_gauntlet_annotations.py, desks/mt5/tests/test_hourly_frontier_search.py
(all pass). ruff and mypy error counts on the file are unchanged.

